-- Seed for the four registers (migration 018).
--
-- RISKS ARE EXTRACTED, NOT WRITTEN. Every row below comes from the Risk
-- Register document already indexed for that project, so the register and
-- the document cannot disagree — open the document, ask the assistant, get
-- the same risks. The six documents use six different sets of column
-- headers, which is why extraction was by header synonym.
--
-- `risk_level` bands the document's 1-25 score (probability x impact):
-- 15+ عالٍ, 8-14 متوسط, below that منخفض. The precise score stays in the
-- document, which is where a reader would look for it.
--
-- `due_date` is populated ONLY where a document states a target resolution
-- date — PRJ-03 alone does. Everywhere else it is NULL, so the assistant
-- answers "not recorded" rather than reporting a date nobody wrote. The
-- sheet marks dueDate required; a real SPM will supply it.
--
-- ISSUES, CHANGE REQUESTS AND DELIVERABLES have no source document in the
-- corpus, so they are authored here — anchored to each project's real
-- status, start and end dates, like the rest of the mock data. Deliverable
-- dates are derived from the project's own span, so a delayed project has
-- late deliverables and a completed one does not.
--
-- Counts: 64 risks, 21 issues, 12 change
-- requests, 27 deliverables.

